      "On science questions, it didn't. At 25%, confidence routing scored 52.8% against 52.6% for random, while the big model alone scored 76.2%. Only the small model's most confident fifth stood out: it was wrong 24% of the time there, and 56% to 68% in every other fifth. Sending up half, confidence pulled 3.2 points ahead of random.",
